      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Vertical Increments and Non-Functional Upgradation (NFU)</h2>
        <p>
          Officers in Levels 10 to 14 progress through both vertical cell steps and cadre-wide financial protections:
        </p>
        <div class="callout-box">
          <h4>The Non-Functional Upgradation (NFU) Mechanism:</h4>
          <p>
            Introduced following the 6th CPC recommendations, <strong>Non-Functional Upgradation (NFU)</strong> ensures that when an IAS officer of a particular batch is posted to a senior position (such as Joint Secretary in Level 14), eligible Group 'A' officers of other organized central services (IRS, IA&amp;AS, IDAS, CPWD engineers) of the same batch receive financial upgradation to that higher pay level on a non-functional basis, even if no promotional post is vacant in their own cadre.
          </p>
          <p>
            This safeguard decouples career financial progression from batch-size stagnation, maintaining financial equity across all branches of civil governance.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Transport Allowance Band 1 vs Staff Car Facility (Level 14+)</h2>
        <p>
          Compensation rules establish a clear division regarding daily travel allowances at this executive level:
        </p>
        <ul class="editorial-list">
          <li><strong>Levels 10 to 13 (Band 1 Transport Allowance):</strong> Officers receive the highest standard Transport Allowance rate (7th CPC base of ₹7,200 in Higher TPTA cities; projected to expand to <strong>₹11,520 to ₹12,960 per month</strong> under the 8th CPC). This base allowance attracts full compounding with Dearness Allowance ($TA + [TA \times DA\%]$).</li>
          <li><strong>Level 14 and Above (The Staff Car Option):</strong> Under Department of Expenditure guidelines, officers in Pay Level 14 (Joint Secretary) and above are offered an institutional choice:
            <ul class="sub-list">
              <li>They may utilize an allocated <strong>official government staff car</strong> for commuting between residence and office.</li>
              <li>Alternatively, they may opt out of the vehicle pool and draw cash Transport Allowance at the enhanced executive rate (7th CPC baseline of ₹15,750 &plus; DA; projected to expand to <strong>₹28,350 to ₹31,500 &plus; DA per month</strong> under the 8th CPC).</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

